  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vinod Kumar Vyas vs The State Of Telangana on 12 November, 2021 Author: Shameem Akther Bench: Shameem Akther The Hon'Ble Dr. Justice Shameem Akther Criminal Petition No.8237 Of 2021 Order:",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "3. The learned counsel for the petitioner/A2 would submit that facts and circumstances of the case on hand are akin to the facts and circumstances of the cases in Crime No.34 of 2018 on the file of Manakondur Police Station and the proceedings in the said case were [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court, vide common order dated 27.08.2018 passed in Criminal Petition No.3731 of 2018 and batch. The contents in the subject case also do not constitute the offences under Sections 188 and 273 of IPC and Section 59(i) of FSS Act against the petitioner/A2 and ultimately prayed to allow the Criminal Petition as prayed for. 4. The learned Assistant Public Prosecutor has fairly conceded the submissions made by the learned counsel for the petitioner/A2.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. The learned counsel for the petitioner/A2 would submit that facts and circumstances of the case on hand are akin to the facts and circumstances of the cases in Crime No.34 of 2018 on the file of Manakondur Police Station and the proceedings in the said case were [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court, vide common order dated 27.08.2018 passed in Criminal Petition No.3731 of 2018 and batch. The contents in the subject case also do not constitute the offences under Sections 188 and 273 of IPC and Section 59(i) of FSS Act against the petitioner/A2 and ultimately prayed to allow the Criminal Petition as prayed for. 4. The learned Assistant Public Prosecutor has fairly conceded the submissions made by the learned counsel for the petitioner/A2.",
